senses.gloss:
(I)--an under world and the residence of Bali: represents the two knees of the Lord;
1: भा. II. 1. २७; 5. ४०; V. २४. 7 & १८; VIII. १३. १४.
Built by विश्वकर्मन्. Bali was sent to this as punishment but was pleased with it: the great cave which Bali and प्रह्लाद entered;
2: Ib. VIII. २२. ३२; २३. 3 & 9, ११-12.
reached by कृष्ण and राम to recover their brothers killed by Kamsa; Bali then as Indrasena welcomed them;
3: Ib. X. ८५. ३४-38.
पातालम्, assigned to Bali by वामन.
4: M. २४६, ६९, ७५-9; Vi. II. 5. 2-3.

(I)--versed in पुराणस्, इतिहासस्, and धर्म- शास्त्रस्, and their expounder addressed by ऋषिस्, शौनक and others. Insulted by बलराम;
1: भा. I. 1. 5-9; २२. 4. 2; X. ७८. २३; M. 1. 4; २३. 1.
रोमहर्षण, the pupil of व्यास narrated the पुराण to the sages assembled for the sacrifice at कुरुक्षेत्र;
2: Br. II. 1. १५; १३. ४१; २४. 3; ३०. 5; III. 9. ३६; ६७. 2; IV. 1. 1; 2. ६९, 7.
addressed as Muni, Sattama, महा- buddhi and Brahmasuta.
3: M. ११३. ५८; १२५. 3; १४६. 2; १८०. 3.
